  "exact-or-prefix-cut": "Every must mention has a predicted span with the same end and a start that is the mention's start, or one letter later when that letter is a prefix letter (מבלוהשכ: cut only by a prefix letter). Glued fails (PLAN.md 4.5): a span that starts earlier, including one that takes in the recorded prefix letter (bench/spans.js counts that glued-left; docs/measurements.md: 37 such spans the cleaner could not peel), or that runs into another word or punctuation. A span glued only by the recorded prefix is reported apart as glued-prefix, so the table can be read both ways, but it does not pass. No predicted span may overlap a must:false mention. The span's type is not checked; a kind mismatch is reported apart.",
  "covers-core": "Some predicted span covers the mention's core (the identifying words) and lies inside the mention plus its recorded prefix. No predicted span may overlap a must:false mention.",
